                <pb facs="0655" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/2059: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-13T21:00:00-04:00">February 13, 1942—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. Your 414, February 11, 1942, 10 p.m. Navy inquires whether the consent of
                    the Brazilian Navy Department applies also to the British Naval vessels. It is
                    important that they should be included in this permission as they constitute an
                    integral part of the naval patrol.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
